WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.103
 Weslie, Kevin,
congratulations.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.872
You smiths are in the
third and final round

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.307
of this competition.

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:09.041
Now, when you came here,
we had you forge signature

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:10.376
blades to a nautical theme.

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:12.077
Now, we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:12.177 --> 00:00:15.248
to recreate this iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:23.623
That is the pira.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.192
And I can tell by the look
of feara on your faces,

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.993
you're not looking
forward to this one.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.562
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.964
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:32.865
 Good luck, man.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:33.500
 Good luck on you too.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:40.939
This day one and we're about
to get started on this pira.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.441
I'm going to be
making a Damascus.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.242
It looks pretty.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.477
Shows a bit of skill.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.579
And I'm hoping that
this Damascus will

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.147
beat out a monosteel blade.

00:00:48.213 --> 00:00:50.449
OK, and into the forge we go.

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:53.987
I'm using 10 84 and 15
and 20 for my billets.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.255
As I'm forge loading it,
I'm looking for the scale

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.524
to start coming
off as big flakes,

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:01.093
because that means that
they've all welded together.

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:04.130
I'm going back between the
forge, the power hammer.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.865
It's hot, very hot.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.400
It's the end of day one.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.101
I've got my build
all forged out,

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:10.903
but it's still really rough.

00:01:10.969 --> 00:01:12.772 line:7%
Still got a lot of work to do.

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:16.042 line:7%
[music playing]

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.576
 So I'm back in
Ozark, Missouri,

00:01:17.676 --> 00:01:19.779
in the shop I share with
other local knivesmiths here.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:23.582
And I'm going to be making
and working on the pira.

00:01:23.682 --> 00:01:26.820
Most of the knives that I
make stop at the longest,

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.153
like, eight inches.

00:01:28.253 --> 00:01:31.657
So just the size of
it is rather daunting.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.126
The smell of propane.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.760
I want to be able to bring
something to the judges

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.162
that they will say, wow.

00:01:37.262 --> 00:01:40.366
So I decide to go with
a Damascus pattern.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:45.170
I am going to use
10 84 and 15 and 20.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.972
I'm going to make a
handful of small billets

00:01:47.072 --> 00:01:48.607
that I will eventually combine.

00:01:48.707 --> 00:01:50.877
One giant billet would be
really hard to work with.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:55.314
So I want to make the smaller
billets to make it manageable.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:58.918
I need the clean up the
faces that will be touching,

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:01.787
simply because it'll
help for a cleaner weld.

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:05.091
At the end of day one, I have
five tiny billets that I will

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:06.626
be able to start with day two.

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:10.630
Put those together, and that
will be the basis for my sword.

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:13.967 line:7%
It looked awesome.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.402 line:0%
 Start of day three,
I got my handle shaped.

00:02:16.468 --> 00:02:19.706
And I've even gotten a chance
to start carving on it.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.941
Today's agenda is heat treats.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.776
Hopefully, I'll be able
to keep it straight.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.482
I pulled out the quench.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:30.883
There's a little
bit of warp in it.

00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:34.086
It's pulling off to the right.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:36.122
Son of a gun.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.590
I open up the oven.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:38.391
I take out the blade.

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:41.060
And the entire blade's cracked.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:41.961
[beep] me.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:42.795
[beep] me.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.764
[beep] me.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:45.765
This blade's done.

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:53.072
It must have been under so much
stress that it just snapped.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:55.909
It's time to get forging again.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.578
Plan B is to just
go on the monosteel.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:01.914
I don't have time to make
another billet of Damascus.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.283
Just adrenaline pumping
through me right about now.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.985
It's just go, go, go.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.653
I would have liked
to have not broken

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.055
the blade I've been
kind of working

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.523
on for the past two days.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.193
But got another blade
forged out in record time.

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:18.230 line:0%
 Ended up taking
me a lot longer

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.299 line:7%
to draw out my Damascus billet.

00:03:20.365 --> 00:03:22.835
I've spent two full
days making the steel

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:24.604
I need to even make this pira.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:28.174
Today, I'm just nervous about
getting this blade done.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.875
I need to get this thing shaped.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:31.243
I start to work in my swell.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.413
But as I continue
to stretch my metal,

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:39.619
I'm noticing that it is
getting dangerously thin.

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:43.690
I stick it back to kind of
straighten everything out,

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.759
and I just watch it lean.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:52.632
It won't survive the quench.

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:54.000
It just won't.

00:03:54.066 --> 00:03:58.137
So two and 1/2 days in, I'm
starting over with a monosteel.

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:02.308
I grab my bar of 51 60 and
into the forge it goes.

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:05.812
Having to start over halfway
through day three is--

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.680
it sucks.

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.015
It really sucks.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:13.352 line:0%
But I'm going to push as hard
as I can to get this thing done.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.154 line:7%
 This is our day four.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:16.422
Still got a lot of work to do.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:20.993
I gotta basically
finish the entire knife.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.162
I'm going to fit up the guard.

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:24.697
From there, I just
go into my handle

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.131
and just, you know,
sanding everything,

00:04:26.231 --> 00:04:28.534
making it all nice and smooth.

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:29.368
There you are.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.770
I get on my wire wrap.

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:33.840
I carve a little relief
going from the hole

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.207
to the outside of the handle.

00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:37.609
That way, the wire will
actually lay flush.

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:39.612
I also do a little
trick where I just stick

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:42.582
a little toothpick in there
to kind of mechanically

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:44.049
lock the wire.

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:46.085
I do edge one final time.

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:48.620
And with that, I'm done.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.890
I can't wait to see
what Doug does with it.

00:04:56.862 --> 00:05:00.800 line:0%
 Day four, and I have to make
a pira in basically one day.

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:03.803
I got the profile of
the blade forged out.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.672
I need to finish grinding.

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:06.839
I need to quench.

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:08.675
And I have to put
the handle together.

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:16.982
Pull it out, and it's
warped just a little bit.

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:18.951
At this point, I'll take it.

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:20.486
I start to work on my handle.

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:23.355
This handle is hard to do it
because the tail is coming

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:25.357
off at a really weird angle.

00:05:25.457 --> 00:05:29.562
The fitting of it,
everything takes time

00:05:29.628 --> 00:05:32.164
that I do not have right now.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:35.234
I don't have the
luxury of add pins.

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:37.502
But I've got to get
it stuck together.

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:42.708
So five minute epoxy it is.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:43.642
I'm done.

00:05:43.742 --> 00:05:45.745
There's nothing else I can do.

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:47.013
I'm out of time.

00:05:47.079 --> 00:05:50.216
I'm not turning in exactly
what I wanted to turn in,

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.185
but there's no quit in me.

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:55.387
And because of that, I
have a finished pira.

00:05:55.487 --> 00:05:59.391
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.594
Your piras look
very interesting.

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:04.130
Now it's time to find
out how lethal they are.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.731
To find that out, I
will take your piras

00:06:05.831 --> 00:06:10.302
and deliver some slashes and
hacks on this boar carcass.

00:06:10.402 --> 00:06:11.204
Kevin, you're up first.

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:12.004
You ready for this?

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:12.905
 Oh, yeah.

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:13.639
 Let's do this.

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:17.777
 This is a big hog.

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:18.777
You know, it's got hide.

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:19.445
It's got bones.

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:20.746
It's got meat.

00:06:20.846 --> 00:06:23.182
And I'm going to have
to go through all of it.

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:24.250
Chills down my spine.

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:25.717
Butterflies in my stomach.

00:06:25.817 --> 00:06:27.520
Hopefully, everything
I did will hold up.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:33.926
[music playing]

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:02.754
 All right, Kevin, let's
talk about your pira here.

00:07:02.821 --> 00:07:05.457
You, sir, have captured
the spirit of what

00:07:05.524 --> 00:07:07.360
this weapon is all about.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.728
The flair that you have
there actually really allows

00:07:09.828 --> 00:07:12.597
me to really get a good grip.

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:14.199
You have a forward
weight, but it's

00:07:14.266 --> 00:07:18.404
perfectly placed right where the
sweet spot is, making every cut

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:20.072
very deep.

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:21.340
Nothing wrong with the edge.

00:07:21.407 --> 00:07:24.810
It's still razor sharp,
and it will kill.

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:25.545
 Thank you.

00:07:27.879 --> 00:07:31.149
 All right, Weslie,
ready to chop some pork?

00:07:31.216 --> 00:07:32.150
 Ready as I'll ever be.

00:07:32.217 --> 00:07:33.953
 All right, let's do it.

00:07:34.019 --> 00:07:38.190
 I am quite literally
shaking in my boots.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:39.992
This is a big pig.

00:07:40.058 --> 00:07:42.862
All I can think is, my handle
is going to bust in two.

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:55.741
 I don't see a pin here.

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:58.010
Is there any mechanical
connection at all that's

00:07:58.077 --> 00:08:00.079
holding this right in there?

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:02.782
 I didn't have time.

00:08:02.849 --> 00:08:04.150
 I understand.

00:08:07.953 --> 00:08:10.055
 There's no mechanical
connection here.

00:08:10.122 --> 00:08:14.126
 Usually, when they whisper,
this is a really bad sign.

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:15.427 line:7%
 I don't want to hold back.

00:08:15.527 --> 00:08:17.730 line:0%
Holding back is not a
fair way to test it.

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:29.608
 Weslie, this is always
tough for any smith.

00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:31.977
We understand that the
problems you had at home

00:08:32.044 --> 00:08:35.281
kind of bit you when it came
to finishing that blade.

00:08:35.381 --> 00:08:39.585
Right now, the handle of your
blade is held in place by glue.

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:42.421
There are no mechanical
connections in the handle.

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:44.823
A "Forged in Fire"
champion would make sure

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.660
that their weapon
is made to withstand

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:51.130
pushing a blade to the absolute
limits of what's possible.

00:08:51.196 --> 00:08:54.700
And unfortunately, we can't
engage your weapon like that.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.802
For that reason,
please exit the forge.

00:08:56.903 --> 00:08:58.470
Come on forward.

00:08:58.537 --> 00:08:59.705
 Thank you.

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:01.507
To push as hard as I
felt like I pushed,

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:05.978
and get here and not have
it tested, it's a bummer.

00:09:06.078 --> 00:09:06.979
Good job.

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:10.783
I understand why and
I agree, but I mean,

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:13.052
kind of would have been
cool to at least see it

00:09:13.152 --> 00:09:15.154
bust halfway through a pig.

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:17.823
But I was still able to
at least present something

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:20.392
to them to show them
that I don't quit.

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:21.593
I don't give up.

00:09:21.693 --> 00:09:22.695
And I am very proud
of myself for that.

00:09:25.297 --> 00:09:26.598
 Kevin, congratulations.

00:09:26.665 --> 00:09:28.233
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:28.333 --> 00:09:31.671
And that it's a title that
comes with a check for $10,000.

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:34.239
Good job, my friend.

00:09:34.339 --> 00:09:35.507
You did fantastic work.

00:09:35.608 --> 00:09:36.741
You deserve it.

00:09:36.842 --> 00:09:38.210
Come over here and
shake our hands.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:40.413
 To everybody who's ever
dogged me, you know, here I am.

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:42.848
I'm standing champion
of "Forged in Fire."

00:09:42.914 --> 00:09:45.317
I would've liked to have
gotten through all three tests.

00:09:45.383 --> 00:09:48.987
But I've proven that not only
do I make the stuff I make,

00:09:49.054 --> 00:09:50.655
but I make it pretty
damn good as well.

00:09:50.722 --> 00:09:52.959
I just won "Forged in Fire."

00:09:53.025 --> 00:09:58.197
[laughs] Oh, man.

